# Source videos: ignore ALL by default (fail-safe). The published site only needs
# the short-form sources (IG / TikTok / YouTube Shorts) that the lightbox plays as
# local mp4s; long-form YouTube sources are huge and only seed hover previews
# locally (the live site uses the YT embed).
#
# This is a pattern, NOT a per-file denylist, on purpose: the old denylist named 17
# long-form files one by one, so any NEW long-form pull was committable by default.
# On 2026-08-21 that had grown to 516 MB of untracked long-form sitting one
# `git add -A` away from blowing the 1 GB GitHub Pages limit (501 MB -> 1238 MB).
#
# Already-tracked sources stay tracked (gitignore never untracks), and the editor's
# publish sweep force-adds the assets projects.js actually references, so curated
# short-form still ships. See _handle_publish in scripts/editor-server.py.
videos/source/*.mp4
videos/source/*.part

